## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | BLOCKING | scripts/ci-sign | 🚨 blocking tmp is expanded before it is assigned — the wwdr import branch crashes ci sign install outright on its first real run scripts ci sign runs under set euo pipefail scripts ci sign 58 but this new block sits before tmp mktemp d scripts ci sign 287 at line 283 tmp wwdr pem expands while tmp is still unset so the first time the guard actually triggers — a keychain with no wwdr certificate i e exactly the first run this pr targets — bash aborts before curl even starts scripts ci sign line 283 tmp unbound variable exit 1 verified by reproducing the exact control flow if guard fails then curl fssl url o tmp wwdr pem fi under set euo pipefail → aborts with tmp unbound variable assigning tmp before the block → proceeds consequences the wwdr g6 import can never succeed through this script — the guard keeps missing so the crash repeats on every install until someone imports the cert manually the feature is dead on arrival every ci sign install on a host without the cert dies — including the per build re verification installs in build macos yml 587 1016 1150 build mobile yml 1162 and host signing provision yml — a full signing outage on the pool install label force the documented recovery path is bricked it deletes the keychain scripts ci sign 271 ensure keychain recreates it empty the guard triggers → crash static gates stay green which is why the pr s verification bash n clean missed it bash n is syntax only and shellcheck raises no sc2154 because tmp does get assigned later in the same case block only a runtime set u trip exposes it fix move the whole block below tmp mktemp d and the consolidated exit trap scripts ci sign 287 290 that also gives wwdr pem exit cleanup for free — at its current position even a working download would escape the rm rf tmp cleanup |
| F2 | open | IMPORTANT | scripts/ci-sign | ⚠️ important the idempotency guard matches any apple worldwide developer relations certificate — an older or expired generation permanently suppresses the g6 import security find certificate a c matches on the certificate s name attribute as an unanchored regex and does not consider validity every wwdr intermediate generation shares the same cn apple worldwide developer relations certification authority so a single g3 g4 g5 intermediate — including a long expired one — in this keychain makes the guard succeed and the g6 import is silently skipped forever that is not hypothetical for this keychain the same script documents the mechanism scripts ci sign 311 gh 2008 note xcode s export allowprovisioningupdates silently imports apple issued certs into the persistent keychain p12 imports can carry the export time chain as well whatever generation those paths bring in is not necessarily g6 — and the failure mode is silent codesign verification chains that need g6 start failing with unable to build chain exactly the class of breakage this pr exists to prevent on a fresh empty keychain the guard behaves correctly which is why this is not a blocking fix guard on the specific certificate not the shared cn substring — compare the apple published g6 sha 1 serial e g dump security find certificate a p kc pem and match the fingerprint or match the hash attribute in find certificate output before skipping the import |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

// PR#2295 review (ai-teammate BLOCKING + IMPORTANT threads) — the WWDR G6
// import block in scripts/ci-sign must (a) run AFTER TMP is assigned and
// the consolidated EXIT trap is installed, and (b) skip the import only
// when the G6 generation itself is present, not any WWDR generation.
//
//   BLOCKING: the block originally sat before TMP="$(mktemp -d)", so the
//     very first guard trigger aborted `install` under `set -u`
//     ("TMP: unbound variable") — the feature was dead on arrival and
//     every cert-less host's install crashed. bash -n and ShellCheck stay
//     green on that shape (TMP is assigned later in the same case block),
//     so only a position assert guards it statically; the runtime repro
//     (stub security/curl, set -euo pipefail) is in the PR thread reply.
//   IMPORTANT: `find-certificate -a -c "Apple Worldwide Developer
//     Relations"` matches ANY generation by shared CN — a single old
//     G3/G4/G5 (even expired, e.g. dragged in by Xcode export, gh-2008
//     mechanism) permanently suppressed the G6 import. The guard now
//     compares each match's SHA-1 (-Z output) against the pinned
//     Apple-published G6 fingerprint (AppleWDRCAG6.cer, OU=G6,
//     2021-03-17 → 2036-03-19).
import 'dart:io';

import 'package:test/test.dart';

void main() {
  final script = File('scripts/ci-sign').readAsStringSync();

  group('PR#2295 WWDR G6 guard', () {
    test('import block runs after TMP assignment and EXIT trap', () {
      final tmpAssign = script.indexOf('TMP="\$(mktemp -d)"');
      final trap = script.indexOf("trap 'rm -rf \"\$TMP\"");
      final block = script.indexOf('WWDR_G6_SHA1=');
      final tmpUse = script.indexOf('"\$TMP/wwdr.pem"');
      expect(tmpAssign, greaterThan(-1), reason: 'TMP assignment missing');
      expect(trap, greaterThan(-1), reason: 'EXIT trap missing');
      expect(block, greaterThan(tmpAssign),
          reason: 'WWDR block must sit below TMP= (set -u crash otherwise)');
      expect(block, greaterThan(trap),
          reason: 'WWDR block must sit below the EXIT trap (wwdr.pem cleanup)');
      expect(tmpUse, greaterThan(tmpAssign),
          reason: '"\$TMP/wwdr.pem" must never expand before TMP is set');
    });

    test('idempotency guard pins the G6 SHA-1, not the shared WWDR CN', () {
      // The real fingerprint of https://www.apple.com/certificateauthority/
      // AppleWWDRCAG6.cer (OU=G6, 2021-03-17 → 2036-03-19), verified by
      // downloading the cert and hashing it (openssl x509 -fingerprint -sha1).
      const g6Sha1 = '0BE38BFE21FD434D8CC51CBE0E2BC7758DBF97B';
      expect(script, contains('WWDR_G6_SHA1="$g6Sha1"'),
          reason: 'G6 fingerprint pin missing or wrong');
      expect(
        script,
        contains('security find-certificate -a -Z -c '
            '"Apple Worldwide Developer Relations"'),
        reason: 'guard must list matches with -Z (SHA-1 per cert)',
      );
      expect(script, contains('| tr -d \' :\' | grep -qi "\$WWDR_G6_SHA1"'),
          reason: 'guard must compare the normalized hash against the pin');
    });
  });
}

// fa-m5 WasmRun host warm cache — the owner provisioned persistent
// CI-authentic zips in ~/vendor-cache/ on the runner box (launchd
// refresher). These asserts pin how the workflows consume that cache
// WITHOUT breaking the incident guards that predate it:
//
//   gh-2233 (wasmrun_restore_temp_race_test): the arch-less shared
//     /tmp/WasmRun.xcframework.zip path must not appear ANYWHERE in the
//     iOS step — so the seed source is ONLY ~/vendor-cache/, never /tmp.
//   gh-1759 (wasmrun_restore_budget_test): build-macos.yml must not
//     contain `rm -f "$ZIP"` before the download loop, and its first
//     occurrence must be the post-loop self-heal purge — so the seed
//     verifies a CANDIDATE file and only `mv`s it onto "$ZIP" when the
//     pinned sha256 matches; a bad candidate is discarded by its own
//     name, never by touching the partial.
//
//   AC1  iOS seeds from ~/vendor-cache/ only (no /tmp reference), via
//        the candidate+mv pattern, before the digest-valid skip.
//   AC2  iOS keeps $RUNNER_TEMP as the only download target.
//   AC3  macOS keeps per-arch /tmp partials and seeds cold ones from
//        ~/vendor-cache/$(basename "$ZIP") via the same candidate+mv
//        pattern (no `rm -f "$ZIP"` in the seed hunk).
import 'dart:io';

import 'package:test/test.dart';

void main() {
  final mobile = File('.github/workflows/build-mobile.yml').readAsStringSync();
  final macos = File('.github/workflows/build-macos.yml').readAsStringSync();

  group('WasmRun host warm cache', () {
    test('AC1 iOS seeds from vendor-cache via digest-verified candidate+mv', () {
      final seed = mobile.indexOf('SEED="\$HOME/vendor-cache/WasmRun.xcframework.zip"');
      expect(seed, greaterThan(-1), reason: 'iOS vendor-cache seed missing');
      final mobileStep = mobile.substring(mobile.indexOf('Restore vendored WasmRun'));
      expect(mobileStep.contains('/tmp/WasmRun.xcframework.zip'), isFalse,
          reason: 'gh-2233: the arch-less /tmp path must not appear at all');
      expect(mobile, contains('SEED_CANDIDATE="\$ZIP.host-seed"'));
      expect(mobile, contains('mv "\$SEED_CANDIDATE" "\$ZIP"'),
          reason: 'only a digest-valid candidate lands on \$ZIP');
      expect(mobile, contains('rm -f "\$SEED_CANDIDATE"'),
          reason: 'bad candidates are discarded by their own name');
      final skip = mobile.indexOf('Complete, digest-valid \$ZIP already present');
      expect(skip, greaterThan(seed),
          reason: 'seed must land before the digest-valid skip check');
    });

    test('AC2 iOS never writes a shared /tmp path', () {
      final step = mobile.substring(mobile.indexOf('Restore vendored WasmRun'));
      expect(step, contains('ZIP="\$RUNNER_TEMP/WasmRun.xcframework.zip"'));
      expect(step, isNot(contains('-o "/tmp/')),
          reason: 'curl output must stay job-private (gh-2233)');
    });

    test('AC3 macOS keeps per-arch partials + candidate+mv vendor-cache seed', () {
      expect(macos, contains('ZIP="/tmp/WasmRun.xcframework-\${{ matrix.arch }}.zip"'),
          reason: 'per-arch resume paths (gh-1759) must stay');
      expect(macos, contains('SEED="\$HOME/vendor-cache/\$(basename "\$ZIP")"'),
          reason: 'cold-/tmp vendor-cache seed fallback missing');
      expect(macos, contains('mv "\$SEED_CANDIDATE" "\$ZIP"'));
      final seedHunk = macos.substring(macos.indexOf('SEED="\$HOME/vendor-cache/'));
      final loopStart = macos.indexOf('for attempt in 1 2 3 4');
      final seedBeforeLoop = seedHunk.substring(0, seedHunk.length > 900 ? 900 : seedHunk.length);
      expect(loopStart, greaterThan(0));
      expect(seedBeforeLoop, isNot(contains(r'rm -f "$ZIP"')),
          reason: 'gh-1759: the seed hunk must never rm the partial itself');
    });
  });
}

